            <ArticleTitle>Netherton's Syndrome.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>135-136</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 6 year old Libyan boy had diffuse erythema at birth and later developed pruritic, maculo-papular, papular, circinat c, double-edge, scaly lesions, suggestive of ichthyosis linearis circumflexa (ILC).Hisscalp hair were brittle and sparse with partial patchy alopecia, showing change of trichorrhexis invaginata, these -associations being characteristic of Netherton's syndrome. The boy had slightly stunted growth; a feature which has not been recorded in previously reported cases.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
